   "fig_label": "Fig. 1",
   "caption": ". XFM-generated elemental maps of a control wheat leaf (A–H) and an age-matched Ptr-infected wheat leaf (I–P), harvested 8 days post-inoculation (dpi). (A, I) Light image of the region of the leaf scanned, (B, J) Compton scatter map of leaf density, (C, K) K, (D, L) Ca, (E, M) Mn, (F, N) Fe, (G, O) Cu, and (H, P) Zn elemental maps. The necrotic (Nec.) and chlorotic (Chl.) zones forming the symptomatic zone are indicated by a dashed white line with the asymptomatic (Asy.) zone defined outside this region (A). Each map is false coloured to help visualize the patterns of elemental distribution, with colour maps provided. To best highlight the Cu distribution in mycelia, a binary colour scale was used (i.e. 1000–1000). Scale bar=1 mm, and elemental maps are expressed in units of ng cm –2.",
